{"id":5896,"date":"2019-06-24T13:18:50","date_gmt":"2019-06-24T17:18:50","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=5896"},"modified":"2019-06-24T13:18:58","modified_gmt":"2019-06-24T17:18:58","slug":"glacier-national-park","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2019\/06\/24\/glacier-national-park\/","title":{"rendered":"Glacier National Park"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>While Kathy and I were working (volunteering) at the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.recreation.gov\/camping\/campgrounds\/233489\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"USACE Fort Peck Montana Downstream Campground (opens in a new tab)\">USACE Fort Peck Montana Downstream Campground<\/a>, we took a few days to visit Glacier National Park.  Although we could have driven to the park, we decided it would be fun to take the Amtrak train.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The <a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Amtrak Empire Builder (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"https:\/\/www.amtrak.com\/empire-builder-train\" target=\"_blank\">Amtrak Empire Builder<\/a> runs daily from Chicago to Seattle and back again.  The number 7 train runs westbound through Glasgow Montana at about noon daily and delivers to Whitefish (W. Glacier area) about 9pm.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"361\" src=\"https:\/\/i1.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/AmtrakTripMap.jpg?fit=685%2C326&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5898\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/AmtrakTripMap.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/AmtrakTripMap-300x143.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/AmtrakTripMap-768x365.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/AmtrakTripMap-1024x487.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/AmtrakTripMap-685x326.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>The &#8220;Empire Builder&#8221; route from Glasgow to Whitefish<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The return (number 8 train) runs eastbound daily and departs Whitefish at 7:30am arriving back in Glasgow around 3:30pm.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Round trip tickets are $108 each, a rental car (2019 Chevy Malibu) cost us $35\/day and the room at a nice new Best Western (w\/ king bed, fridge, microwave) was $94\/day.  Although the trip by train is more than driving in our own car, the trip was far more relaxing and enjoyable.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Riding on the train allows you the opportunity to move around at will from your car to either the lounge car, the panorama view sightseeing car, or the formal dining car.  They have sleeping cars too, but we didn&#8217;t have an opportunity to see those.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Remember, you can click on any of the thumbnails below to see an enlarged image<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i2.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_084540.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5899\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5899\" class=\"wp-image-5899\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_084540.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_084540-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_084540-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_084540-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_084540-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_084540-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>Our comfy seats<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_110750.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5900\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5900\" class=\"wp-image-5900\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_110750.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_110750-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_110750-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_110750-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_110750-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_110750-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>The Sightseeing Car<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_122522.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5901\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5901\" class=\"wp-image-5901\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_122522.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_122522-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_122522-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_122522-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_122522-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190530_122522-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>The Lounge Car<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Renting the car (with unlimited mileage) we were able to drive just under 600 miles in 2 days seeing both West Glacier and East Glacier.  We were not, unfortunately able to take the &#8220;Going to The Sun Road&#8221; all the way across from west to east because 22 miles of the road were still closed due to not being cleared of snow yet (this was the end of May!).  As a result (as you&#8217;ll see in the video below) we had to take Route 2 the long way around the bottom of the park from one side to the other.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed-youtube wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Our Train Trip to Glacier National Park   herbnkathyrv\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/e5D5sWfK-dI?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen><\/iframe>\n<\/div><figcaption>Our Amtrak Trip to Glacier May 2019<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Thanks for riding along with us on our adventures.  Soon after our Amtrak ride to Glacier (celebrating our 45th anniversary) we packed up our coach at Fort Peck and moved on east to our next Workamping\/Volunteer gig at Spearfish, SD.  Post on our experiences there follows shortly.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you&#8217;re not already subscribed to this blog,  you can easily do so by scrolling up to the top of any page and entering your email address in the block on the right side.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can also subscribe to our YouTube channel (<a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"herbnkathyrv (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/results?search_query=herbnkathyrv\" target=\"_blank\">herbnkathyrv<\/a>) on You Tube.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you&#8217;re curious (at any time) to know where we are at that moment then click the button at the top right of this page labeled &#8220;<a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"See Where We Are Now (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"http:\/\/aprs.link\/app\/aprs\/stations\/googlemap-WB8BHK-9\" target=\"_blank\">See Where We Are Now<\/a>&#8220;.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We&#8217;d love to hear from you.  If you scroll all the way down to the bottom of this page, you can send us a note.  Again, thanks for riding along.  &#8217;til next time &#8211; safe travels.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p> <\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Recap of our Amtrak train trip to Glacier National Park celebrating our 45th wedding anniversary in late May 2019.  Pictures and Video<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":5961,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[91,264,19546,554707329],"tags":[554707511,554707753,554707749,554707759,554707746,554707741,554707752,554707494,554707747,3559,297133,1062728,218575385,554707751,554707750,554707748],"class_list":["post-5896","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-blogging","category-learning","category-sightseeing","category-traveling","tag-campground","tag-downstream-campground","tag-east-glacier","tag-flathead-lake","tag-glacier","tag-glasgow","tag-lake-mcdonald","tag-motorhome","tag-national-park","tag-rv","tag-rv-camping","tag-rv-lifestyle","tag-rvillage","tag-usace","tag-west-glacier","tag-whitefish"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/5896","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=5896"}],"version-history":[{"count":9,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/5896\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":5964,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/5896\/revisions\/5964"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/5961"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=5896"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=5896"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=5896"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}